.TH WELLMOD 1 "September 2026" "wellutils 1.4.0-55" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
wellmod \- list loaded kernel modules with their sizes and dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellmod
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellmod
.PP
Lists loaded kernel modules with their sizes and dependencies,
grouped by usage count.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-deps " MODULE"
Show the dependencies of \fIMODULE\fR from \fImodules.dep\fR (dashes and
underscores are equivalent). If the module is unknown or
\fImodules.dep\fR is missing, the box view reports it and the JSON view
prints \fB"found": false\fR; both exit with status \fB1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter ", " \-f " PATTERN"
Only list modules whose name matches \fIPATTERN\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
\fB\-\-deps\fR: module not found (also with \fB\-\-json\fR).
.TP
.B 2

Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1)
